# DanNet SHACL shapes: EDITORIAL rules for newly edited data.
#
# Stricter requirements than base.ttl, meant ONLY for targeted validation of
# individual focus nodes touched by an edit (see `validate-node`) before a
# write is committed. Legacy data is deliberately exempt: e.g. ≈70k imported
# OEWN synsets legitimately lack a wn:definition, so running these against the
# full graph would drown signal in noise.
#
# A deliberately small starter set; extend as editorial policy is decided.
#
# NOTE: property shapes are deliberately given explicit IRIs (rather than the
# usual blank nodes) so that validation reports can group violations by a
# stable shape identity.

@prefix sh:      <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix ontolex: <http://www.w3.org/ns/lemon/ontolex#> .
@prefix wn:      <https://globalwordnet.github.io/schemas/wn#> .
@prefix dns:     <https://wordnet.dk/dannet/schema/> .

## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## LexicalConcept (synset): edited synsets should carry a definition.
## sh:Warning: surfaces in the editing UI without blocking the write.
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dns:EditorialConceptShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass ontolex:LexicalConcept ;
    sh:property dns:EditorialConceptShape-definition .

dns:EditorialConceptShape-definition a sh:PropertyShape ;
    sh:path wn:definition ;
    sh:minCount 1 ;
    sh:severity sh:Warning ;
    sh:message "An edited synset should have a wn:definition." .
